<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Artavasdes I of Media Atropatene</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 20 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Artavasdes I was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/media-atropatene">Media Atropatene</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> in the first century BCE. Allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthia">Parthia</a>, he helped defeat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a>'s campaign of 36 BCE, when Antony's siege train was destroyed and his siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phraaspa">Phraaspa</a> failed. Quarrelling with the Parthian king, he then allied with Antony, betrothing his daughter to Antony's son Alexander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/helios">Helios</a>, and later took refuge with Augustus.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/artavasdes-i-of-media-atropatene.jpg" alt="Artavasdes I of Media Atropatene" width="320" height="153" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ArtavasdesICoinMedia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
